1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,910
So the first thing you need to do is to read reading is the first step in this three step structure.
所以，你首先需要做的就是阅读；阅读是这个三步结构里的第一步。

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:17,520
Reading is a fantastic way to fill your mind with new ideas to learn new vocabulary rich vocabulary good structure good sentence structure and structure of ideas as well.
阅读是让头脑充满新想法、学习丰富的新词汇，以及良好句式和观点结构的好方法。

3
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:21,600
And it's essential if you want to learn how to organize your thoughts better.
如果你想学习更好地组织思想，她认为这很重要。

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,749
Because you can learn how other people organize their ideas and organize their thoughts.
因为你可以学习别人怎样组织观点、怎样安排思路。

5
00:00:25,759 --> 00:00:32,160
So every time you read a book whether it's fiction or non fiction you expose yourself to all of these things.
所以，每次读书，无论是小说还是非虚构作品，你都在接触这些内容。

6
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:38,480
There is no way that you could come up with all of this rich vocabulary or good structure on your own.
她认为，你不可能独自想出所有这些丰富词汇和良好结构。

7
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:46,480
And why would you it's not necessary when you can learn from other people who have gone through this process to write those fantastic books.
而且何必这样做呢？既然可以向经历了写作过程、写出优秀作品的人学习，就没有这个必要。

8
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,520
The way I see it is books are really a gateway into the world of organized thoughts and good structure.
在我看来，书籍就是通往有条理的思想和良好结构世界的一扇门。

9
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:59,360
I mean think of how long it takes somebody to write a book how many revisions do they do.
想想看，写一本书需要多久，作者又要修改多少次。

10
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:05,120
How many other people are involved in the process to improve on their ideas or improve on their structure.
还有多少人参与这个过程，帮助完善观点或改进结构。

11
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:09,350
There is a lot of time money and effort put into writing books.
写书这件事投入了大量时间、金钱和精力。

12
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:19,519
You can leverage this and use this final product to enrich your mind with rich vocabulary with good structure and with organized thoughts.
你可以利用这些投入，通过最终的作品，用丰富词汇、良好结构和有条理的思想充实头脑。

13
00:01:19,519 --> 00:01:26,879
You can basically learn from these high level authors or from the higher level work that other people have created.
基本上，你可以向这些高水平作者学习，也可以从别人创作的较高水平作品中学习。

14
00:01:26,879 --> 00:01:34,560
Now what kinds of books should you read well you've probably guessed I'm not talking about comic books I'm not talking about children's books.
那么应该读哪些书呢？你可能猜到了，我指的不是漫画书，也不是儿童读物。

15
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:46,879
The kinds of books I recommend you to read are non fiction or also fiction books biographies classical literature books about historical events business books or literary fiction.
我推荐读的书包括非虚构或虚构作品、传记、经典文学、历史事件相关书籍、商业书籍或文学小说。

16
00:01:46,879 --> 00:01:51,910
All of these are the types of books that have had a lot of work put into them.
这些都是投入了大量工作的书籍类型。

17
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:57,440
That are using a level of vocabulary and structure that you probably want to aim for.
它们使用的词汇和结构水平，可能正是你想努力达到的。

18
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:05,599
Since you are working to become a leader you probably want to sound more intelligent and sound more structured and organized as you speak.
既然你正在努力成为领导者，可能也希望说话听起来更有见识、更有结构、更有条理。

19
00:02:05,599 --> 00:02:13,040
These are the kinds of books that you can use to draw those ideas from and to get the vocabulary from as well.
这些就是你可以从中汲取观点、同时学习词汇的书。

20
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:17,519
I do encourage you to read books that you don't normally read.
我确实鼓励你读一些平时不太会读的书。

21
00:02:17,519 --> 00:02:23,760
This will help to expose you to new ideas new ways of thinking new ways of structuring your ideas as well.
她认为，这会帮助你接触新观点、新思考方式，以及新的观点组织方式。

22
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:29,920
So if you normally read biographies then maybe opt for books about historical events.
所以，如果你平时读传记，也许可以选择历史事件相关书籍。

23
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:36,400
Or maybe if you read business books a lot you can learn a lot by reading classical literature.
又或者，如果你常读商业书籍，也可以通过阅读经典文学学到很多东西。

24
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:40,239
How often should you read this is a question I get asked quite a lot.
应该多久读一次书？这是我经常被问到的问题。

25
00:02:40,239 --> 00:02:43,280
I recommend you read five to ten pages every day.
我建议你每天读五到十页。

26
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:48,960
The way I do it is over breakfast generally as I am eating my breakfast I have a book beside me.
我的做法通常是在吃早餐时读书；吃早餐的时候，我旁边会放一本书。

27
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:52,639
Instead of my phone instead of instagram I have a book beside me.
我身边放的是书，代替手机，代替 Instagram。

28
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:57,510
And I am reading the book going through the pages of the book as I eat my breakfast.
我一边吃早餐，一边读书，一页页地往下看。

29
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:03,040
As to when you read it's really up to you how you like to fit it into your daily schedule.
至于什么时候读，则完全取决于你，取决于你想怎样把阅读安排进日程。

30
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:13,680
But I recommend you read five to ten pages every day this way you are filling your mind with new vocabulary with good sentence structure and new ideas as well.
但我建议每天读五到十页；这样，你就在用新词汇、良好句式和新观点充实头脑。
